<section class="ph"><div class="ph-media"><img class="ph-img" src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-damage-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-damage.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="797" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"></div><div class="wrap ph-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><a href="/mi-cities-served/">Cities</a><i aria-hidden="true">/</i><span aria-current="page">Kalamazoo</span></nav><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Southwest Michigan · Kalamazoo County</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Kalamazoo, Michigan</h1><p class="ph-lede">Kalamazoo has lived through two notable tornadoes in recent memory: the 1980 storm that cut through downtown and the 2024 tornado in neighboring Portage. Its historic neighborhoods, college campuses and growing suburbs all share that storm exposure.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-maize" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ic" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-glass" href="/request-claim-review/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="ph-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Kalamazoo County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Southwest Michigan</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local"><div><p class="local-k">Neighborhoods &amp; areas</p><p>Vine, Stuart, Oakwood, Westnedge Hill, Edison, Northside, Milwood, Winchell, South Street historic district</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Housing mix</p><p>Kalamazoo has Victorian and early-1900s homes in Stuart, Vine and the South Street area, mid-century homes in Milwood and Winchell, student rentals near campus, and newer subdivisions in Portage and Oshtemo.</p></div><div><p class="local-k">Common claim drivers</p><ul class="chips"><li>Tornado damage</li><li>Wind and hail</li><li>Fallen trees</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Basement water</li></ul></div></div>
<h2>Kalamazoo Storm Claims and Independent Appraisal</h2>
<p>Southwest Michigan sits in the path of storms moving in from the west, and Kalamazoo County has felt their force more than once. Its housing ranges from 19th-century homes in the Stuart and Vine neighborhoods to mid-century ranches in Milwood and Winchell and newer subdivisions in Portage and Oshtemo Township. Each type brings its own claim issues after a storm.</p>
<h3>1980 and 2024: two tornadoes, two eras</h3>
<p>On May 13, 1980, a tornado moved directly through downtown Kalamazoo, damaging businesses, homes and the downtown mall area. More than four decades later, on May 7, 2024, a tornado struck Portage, just south of the city, damaging homes, businesses and a mobile home community. The 2024 storm produced a wave of claims in which homeowners and insurers disagreed about the extent of structural damage, the cost of debris removal and whether partial repairs were enough.</p>
<h3>Wind damage is more than the roof</h3>
<p>After a tornado or strong straight-line wind, damage often extends beyond missing shingles. Siding, windows, framing, garage doors, fences and trees can all be affected, and interior water damage may follow. A careful inspection should look for racked framing, lifted roof decking and cracked foundations, not just the obvious exterior damage. Our <a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">windstorm and tornado appraisal</a> service builds a full, documented scope.</p>
<h3>Historic homes and student rentals</h3>
<p>In Vine, Stuart and the South Street historic district, homes have ornate woodwork, original windows and complex rooflines. Repairing them properly costs more, and estimates that apply standard pricing often fall short. Near the university campuses, rental owners face the added challenge of coordinating repairs around tenants and documenting contents that may belong to several people.</p>
<p>Not every Kalamazoo claim comes from a tornado. Summer thunderstorms bring hail and straight-line wind to the county most years, and the Labor Day 1998 derecho knocked down trees across southern Michigan. In winter, lake-effect snow bands from Lake Michigan sometimes reach Kalamazoo, setting up ice dams on older homes with limited attic insulation and ventilation. These losses are often disputed on scope, with insurers and homeowners disagreeing about how much drywall, insulation and roofing needs replacement.</p><p>Newer subdivisions in Portage and Oshtemo Township face mostly hail and wind claims, often centered on whether a damaged roof can be repaired or must be replaced to achieve a uniform result.</p>
<div class="note"><b class="h">Document early</b>After a tornado or windstorm, take photos and video before cleanup if it’s safe to do so. Keep damaged materials if you can, and save receipts for emergency repairs.</div>
<p>If you’re deciding whether to dispute your settlement, read our guide on <a href="/great-lakes-claim-guides/michigan-appraisal-clause-explained/">Michigan’s appraisal clause</a>, and use the <a href="/mi-claim-calculators/appraisal-readiness-score/">appraisal readiness score</a> to see whether your documentation is ready.</p>
<h2>Services available in Kalamazoo</h2>
<p>Every Michigan Insurance Appraiser service is available to owners in Kalamazoo and surrounding communities, including:</p>
<ul><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/appraisal-demand-representation/">Appraisal Demand Representation</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/homeowner-claim-appraiser/">Homeowner Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/commercial-condo-hoa-appraisal/">Commercial, Condo &amp; HOA Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/hail-roof-damage-appraisal/">Hail &amp; Roof Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/ice-dam-frozen-pipe-appraisal/">Ice Dam &amp; Frozen Pipe Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/water-sewer-backup-appraisal/">Water &amp; Sewer Backup Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/michigan-claim-appraisal/fire-smoke-loss-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Loss Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Questions from Kalamazoo property owners</h2><div class="qa"><details><summary><span>Do you handle Portage tornado claims?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>Yes. We review estimates and serve as appraisers for homeowners and businesses throughout Kalamazoo County, including Portage and Oshtemo Township.</p></div></details><details><summary><span>Can appraisal include debris removal and tree costs?</span><i class="qa-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i></summary><div class="qa-a"><p>If your policy covers debris and tree removal and the insurer agrees the loss is covered, the cost of those items can be part of the amount of loss decided in appraisal, subject to any policy limits.</p></div></details></div>
